  "description": "The first ever 22\" Front Suspension (100mm travel) Mountain Bike for kids 5-8 years old. Lightweight and high-quality components designed specifically for kids. Perfect for singletrack and technical mountain bike trails.\nYama Jama 22\" bridges the gap between 20\" and 24\" bikes for kids who are too big for a 20\" but not quite tall enough for a 24\"!\nIt all starts with a meticulously designed, lightweight but sturdy 6061-T6 alloy frame using hydroformed and double-butted tubing, a semi-integrated head tube, a unique forged BB shell/yoke for added stiffness, ISCG-05 tabs and even an internal routing option for dropper posts.\nThe Brood Bike Co. Eldorado suspension fork was designed and tuned specifically for young kids and features a hand-laid carbon fibre lower, a replaceable cartridge damper with a rubber bladder, lockout, a 15mm through-axle and 100mm of plush, nearly stiction-free travel.\nWith a base like that, we couldn’t skimp on the components. The drivetrain starts with the Brood Bike Co. Styx 130mm crank using a SRAM pattern direct mount interface for the chainwheel and a sealed external bottom bracket. We add a Brood 30t narrow wide alloy chainwheel and then utilize a SRAM GX derailleur and shifter combo to get things moving to the 11-36T 10-speed SRAM cassette. Stopping is handled by powerful Tektro Auriga hydraulic disc brakes.\nThe next big highlight is the wheelset and tires. The Yama Jama uses Brood Bike Co. tubeless-ready lightweight but highly durable rims with a wide profile and tops it off with the amazing Brood Maxtion foldable, tubeless-ready tire. Touch points matter for kids too, so we’ve topped this Yama Jama off with Brood Tenderiderz lock-on grips.",
